    + ' '
    + 'RE-WALKED 2026-09-28 against Trade Rules.dc.html (Rev .101, rev 2026-09-28.1), batch R1. Built: three readings replace the yellow banners (daemon runs · opportunities in no allocation, click shows only those · gates carried by none, click opens the gate form); picking folds the four columns into a sticky lineage bar (← Back, the path as crumbs, four segments of chips, Whole chain ▾) with the record right under it; every change of focus is pushed to ?pick=&sym=, and Esc / ⌥← / ← Back / the browser all walk one path that truncates rather than loops, restoring each step\u2019s filters, folds, group mode, board sort and scroll; the symbol is a lens across the chain (toolbar field with the book\u2019s tickers, opportunity-card chips, group-header tickers, scope tiles) and is kept when a pick can act on it; records for opportunity (Run by · Gate · Instances · Realised · Won, Enters when, the Scope board with never ran / off scope and Realised/Count/A–Z sort), structure and allocation (with the rules table), symbol (Covered by + Rules that can act on it) and the whole instance column; the list drills #id in place with [ ] stepping through the rows it came from (replace, not pushed). Measured: all counts come from readInstances over the one executions query, so the board, record and bar never disagree. Divergences, each with its reason: (1) the readings count over what Show leaves visible, not the whole book — this page\u2019s standing rule that a count must read the scope the columns draw; (2) Enters when prints the store\u2019s own conditions, and says none recorded where there are none — PROD holds conditions on 1 of 8 opportunities, the prototype\u2019s conditions are illustrative; (3) the table keeps the existing columns (Actions first, Net PnL · Underlying cost · Return % pairs) and Type / Expiry filters where they have more than one value — the prototype draws Status · Since · Group only, and design absence is not deletion; (4) an instance picked here shows its header, step bar and five readings until batch R2 lands the InstanceRecord face; the eye still opens Positions\u2019 sheet until R3.'
