    + ' ' + 'REV .120 (2026-09-30, §17.3): the route now reads the symbol (symbolScope true, matching the design’s new sym flag). The symbol lens step lives at ?symbol= (the old ?sym= still reads), so the top bar and the focus stack share one value: a symbol cell, Back, Release or the chip’s ✕ each write the top bar, and ⌘K swaps the step in place. Arriving, the carried symbol is adopted only if some scope names it or an instance ran on it — the app’s existing test for the lens, one step wider than the design’s “in an opportunity scope”, because a ticker that ran outside its scope still has a lens here; otherwise the page stays unfiltered, the top bar keeps it, and the toolbar says “X is in no scope and ran nowhere”. The Symbol box and its datalist are gone.'
     + ' ' + 'REV .140 (2026-10-01, Package .52 full; the Desk prototype\u2019s Rules view): select = edit. Picking a structure, opportunity or allocation on the chain opens its inspector as well as the lineage and record (the app keeps Rev .101\u2019s fold — the prototype lights the chain in place); picking it again releases both. The allocation\u2019s Edit gate opens the gate set\u2019s inspector in its place; one at a time; Esc closes it before it is Back. The inspector is DS InspectorPanel glass, 8 off the right, 52 from the top, 400 wide; the four edit sheets\u2019 fields live in it and write the whole object (PUT) 500ms after the last change, ⌘Z / the toast undoing on the page\u2019s stack — no scrim, no Save / Cancel; the foot is Delete · Duplicate and Saves as you type · ⌘Z undoes; the gate set\u2019s head says edits go into vN+1 · the daemon keeps vN. The sheets\u2019 field mappings are one module each (allocationForm · opportunityForm · gateForm · structureForm), shared by the New sheets and the inspectors. Delete asks nothing: opportunity, allocation, gate set and an empty trade leave the chain at once and DELETE goes when the toast leaves without Undo (api 0.1.9 / core 0.28.1; Owner 2026-10-01 held delete); refused first, in the server\u2019s words, while in use — an opportunity with trades, the allocation the daemon runs, a gate set an opportunity, an allocation or the daemon points at, a trade with fills. A held opportunity also leaves its allocations, and Undo puts both back. Activate / Deactivate (opportunity, structure), Set active / Clear active (the confirm retires; the daemon reads it on next start), Duplicate (opportunity inactive, structure, gate set — a real copy, opened) are done at once and undone from the toast. New (＋ in a column) is still a sheet. DIVERGED, named: a structure has no Delete — the store has no hard delete and none was approved; Undo of a structure Duplicate takes the copy off the books instead of deleting it. Emergency flatten keeps its confirm (Desk). DIVERGED, named: the gate set\u2019s closing note does not say earnings dates come from the market-data feed — the daemon reads them from the set itself (core settings.get_hedge_config → worker gs_trading / execution_guard), so the inspector keeps the dates under strategy and says so.' + ' ' + 'TD-62 (2026-10-03, Owner chose A on ASK-desk-inspector-endpoint-labels): the second line of the Allocation, Opportunity and Structure inspectors is the request the app makes — `PATCH /api/strategy/strategies/allocations/{id}`, `PATCH …/opportunities/{id}`, `PUT …/structures/{id}` — built from `STRATEGY_WRITES` in api/strategy.ts, which the writers send, and refusals name the same request. Diverges from the prototype’s `PUT /strategy/<kind>`: no service serves that path, /strategy/* is a SPA redirect, and since api 0.6.0 the allocation and opportunity PUTs are gone (PATCH is the edit). Design asked to update the prototype labels and its L750/L765 comments.'
