    + ' '
    + 'SHEET (2026-09-29, rev .94 sheet, walked on local DEV :5173 beside :8099 at 1440 and 1024): the Owner found ＋ Plan a trade opening a one-column form in the reading inspector, the check at the bottom. It is now the prototype\u2019s order sheet: 920 wide off the right edge over a scrim (Esc or ✕ closes, a click outside does not), header sentence, the form left and the live check in a 360 raised column right. BUSINESS FIRST: the check was all \u201cnot computed\u201d, but every reading it needs is one the app already reads \u2014 monitor /status margin facts, the quote feed and latest bar (Positions\u2019 spot resolver), and Room to add\u2019s `regTShortPutMargin` and headroom arithmetic. So a single short put reads Spot (with its source), OTM, Cash secured, Reg-T margin, Est. credit, Pressure now \u2192 after, Max at this strike (with what cash covers) and Free cash after intended; a covered call reads shares held vs needed. `planCheck` is tested on invented accounts. Diverges, named: the ceiling is the trader\u2019s risk level from Backing & Model (Balanced 50% by default), not the prototype\u2019s fixed 70%; a put beyond free cash but under the ceiling reads amber \u201cOn margin\u201d rather than red \u2014 Room to add counts margin-backed puts, and the Owner sells them; spreads and several legs say \u201cNot modelled\u201d rather than run a naked-put formula. Create order intent is drawn and wired: it saves the plan and marks it intended \u2014 this app\u2019s intent is the plan\u2019s status, no order route exists (D10) \u2014 held until the check passes. The left keeps what the store holds beyond the prototype: legs with their own side (never picked for the reader), price effect, target / stop / exit-by and the plan\u2019s expiry; Structure is one field as drawn, with the rulebook structures offered and an exact name linking one. The prototype\u2019s chain quick-picks are still not copied (they fabricate strikes from spot). Also fixed: the account was seeded before /status answered and could submit empty; it now falls back to the default until picked.'
